        <div type="bibliography">
	        <!--bibliography goes here -->
           <p>What is evidently the same decipherment, probably due to S. Tripathy, was first published without diactrical marks in a provisional report on excavations at Udayagiri site 2 (<bibl><ptr target="bib:IAR2001-2002"/></bibl>) and then published with diacritical marks in the final excavation report (<bibl><ptr target="bib:Tripathy+Khamari2012_01"/></bibl>); apparently before the latter version became known to him, K. Tanaka had already published a reading with several improvements based on his identification of the source text that underlies lines 10–19 of the inscription (<bibl><ptr target="bib:Tanaka2014_01"/></bibl>). The results of these previous scholars are reassessed in the present digital edition against a photograph that is good but still leaves several points of doubt.</p>
